s sunday january 26 so what  happened well unfortunately not  everybody got paid in fact a lot of  people didn't get paid some individuals  a few of them among the most publicly  vocal and a few of them who appeared on  record in my last video on the subject  did get their money by sunday and a few  got their money only after the deadline  and after they persistently bothered  management about it but at least they  got it unfortunately many people didn't  including their South American rocket  league team that made the World  Championships in season seven and  Nate last year but they're far from the  only ones as of this recording here are  just some of the people who told me they  haven't got their money social media  managers Brazilian Rainbow six siege  players from the female division  South American rocket league players and  staff designers Brazilian csgo staff na  apex legends players certain Regional  Managers pop G players staff working for  Loki in Korea and more all of those  people were supposed to be paid they  weren't and those are just the people  that I'm in contact with at this point  it seems some former low key players and  staff are starting to take matters into  their own hands for example the manager  of Loki's former Brazilian csgo team  told me that he and a number of other  individuals who formerly worked for Loki  are consulting with a lawyer about  potential legal action and it's worth  noting here guys that since my initial  video came out a ton of people have  reached out to me and told me horror  stories that aren't even related to the  hundred thirty seven thousand dollars  including some that go back to Loki  studio / GG easy the video editing arm  of Loki now I mentioned earlier that  Gerena the company that distributes  League of Legends in Southeast Asia is  looking into the situation basically one  of Loki's most successful teams which is  their League of Legends squad is based  in Vietnam which is of course in that  region  they came 17 xx at Worlds last year I  received information a short time ago  that Gerena and potentially riot games  themselves are putting very serious  pressure on Loki I reached out to Riot  Games to try and discern the nature of  this pressure what is actually going on  behind the scenes and here are a few  statements they sent to me from their  colleagues at Gerena hi Colin thank you  for reaching out it's important to  clarify that Riots interaction with Loki  eSports is in regards to the Loki  eSports team competing in Vietnam in the  League of Legends of Vietnam  championship series the CS we have no  insight into the ongoings of their  global org outside of Vietnam including  Loki teams competing in other games /  eSports Riot Games and Gerena are  publishing partner for League of Legends  in Southeast Asia Taiwan Hong Kong and  Macau worked diligently to ensure that  all teams comply with our global  League operations policies including  upholding financial commitments to their  players I further reached out for more  clarification on what exactly this means  and here's what I got  quote we are working with Loki to ensure  adherence to our global league  operations policies and quote so what  can we take from those statements well  it's tough to tell obviously something  is going on behind the scenes that much  is clear but exactly what Gerena and  riot won't say at this time  but according to information provided to  me by multiple sources with knowledge of  the situation it is entirely possible  that Loki eSports will be kicked out of  the VCS by riot now this particular  information has come to me very recently  should I find out more  should I get a confirmation you'll be  the first to know so what about the  owners of Loki eSports where are they in  all of this well I've been in let's call  it intermittent contact through Twitter  DMS with one of them by the name of Tony  nuyen now Tony is the one who gave me  the latest final repayment deadline that  was Sunday January 26 I reached out to  him about the missing money the blown  deadline and Riot Games and gharanas  involvement in this situation he sent me  the following statement  I personally been dealing with slash  communicating with players slash staff  and working to get their payments out  many of which have already been paid the  management on the Loki eSports side has  been at constant work to get things in  order I am doing what I can do to assist  them since as stated before I run the  marketing and media side more of the  other businesses there are players yet  to be paid but we are covering one team  at a time we are all different companies  from Loki community to Loki eSports but  we help each other regardless I  personally am NOT going anywhere and  will continue to represent this brand  along with a many hard-working staff and  talent the mistakes of one company will  reflect on the others and we understand  that all players and staff are open to  DM me I will continue resolving the  issues every day - every second now he's  not actually an owner but I also reached  out to max wood who during this entire  process has been  the middleman communicating between  low-key management and ownership and  low-key staff and players I asked him  about the blown deadlines for repayment  and what he said to me was quote from  what I've been told  payments have been going out and people  are being paid slowly albeit I've been  sent screenshots and confirmed with some  managers slash teams I also asked him to  confirm some of that more i popping  information about Gerena and Riot Games  involvement now he wouldn't tell me  anything specific but he did acknowledge  the possibility of low-key eSports  being removed from the VCS from League  of Legends in Vietnam now I said earlier  that a group of former players and staff  have been consulting with a lawyer to  see if there's a legal recourse to  everything that's happened to them on  Loki and the legality of this entire  situation has been on my mind throughout  the weeks that I've been reporting on  Josh Marcus of mkm a toronto-based law  firm that specializes in eSports told me  that people who are a part of Loki or  have been who haven't been paid yet  and our owed money could conceivably  have a case so to speak the question as  he pointed out to me is whether or not  it's actually worth it when you're  getting money late you could probably  make an argument that you should be  getting some interest on that you know  we're talking not a lot of interests  maybe 3% over a year that's you know  then brought down to about three months  and you know you're kind of left ok at  what point is it worth pursuing a case  but certainly you know if you're not  paid whatsoever  yeah that's your buddy course your  recourse is to the courts to dispute  resolution to really prove that there is  that breach of contract this is  especially true in the Loki situation  because a lot of the affected people are  pretty young they don't have the money  necessarily to hire a lawyer  they don't have the money to pay for  court filings they don't have the time  to take off work or school to represent  themselves so I asked Josh the eSports  lawyer what do you do if you're 19 years  old you're trying to live the eSports  dream  and something like this happens the  first step is really when you get that  contract before you sign it either have  a lawyer another legal professional and  eSports coach somebody who is very  familiar with the industry and how these  contracts should be written just have a  look at it even if it's a matter of  pointing out what you're agreeing to you  know there's often little red flags that  are hidden in there or things that are  Mis drafted that really could come back  to bite you at the end once you're  already signed in and you're at this  point you know keeping a constant  communication trail keeping things in  writing wherever possible even if that's  discord or text message you know  something that just shows the position  or the situation that you've been put in  all of that can help down the line you  know it's hard to tell how the whole  industry will unfold but certainly you  know there's no reason not to be  protecting your rights at the stage and  then even if it's a matter of writing to  the team and bugging them every month  and saying where's my money you're at  least showing that hey I haven't  forgotten about this you know this this  should be there and if the team's gonna  be successful they're gonna want to make  sure that they're paying you out  otherwise you know they get a lot of bad  press if you ask me who can challenge a  straw Louis yeah Team Liquid yeah  mousesports can give them a little run  for their money I still don't really  fully believe they could be distraught  us in the long term I want to see the  likes of Xero and the likes of simple on  teams on which that enable them to  succeed I want to see them fight a straw  I want to see the ultimate five-man unit  versus the ultimate individual frag fest

